    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Facing an uncontrolled talent drain that crippled its offense, the disorder-plagued franchise of Colorado executed a decisive order-restoration move by firing its coach with eight games left. The crisis manager John Tortorella then imposed order after chaos, guiding a 7-0-1 close and restoring control through playoffs, but the legitimacy-proving stage of the Western Conference Final exposed the team's fragility. On May 26, the order-restoring victor from Vegas consolidated authority with a four-game sweep, holding the league-leading offense to a single goal and claiming a seat at the ultimate table of the Stanley Cup Final.",
